+questeditor.help.text = ARENAMP SERVER QUEST STUDIO\n\nQuests live on the server as JSON files in server/data/custom/quests. The client never edits them directly: every button here sends a command to the server, the server validates it, writes the file and sends the whole model back. Only Moderator (staffRank 1) and Administrator (staffRank 2) can open this window.\n\nOPEN\n  /quests studio - open this window\n  /quests reload - reload definitions from disk\n\nWORKFLOW\n  1. Overview: type an id and a name in the left panel, press New. The id must be lowercase latin letters, digits and underscores.\n  2. Overview: set the quest giver (RefId, cell, optional UniqueIndex) and the initial stage, then Save overview.\n  3. Stages: create every stage you need. Index is the stage number, Journal is the journal text, Dialogue is what the NPC says at this stage. Mark the final stage as Complete (or Fail).\n  4. Dialogue: add the green topic the player clicks, then the offer text and the answer options. An option with action "start" begins the quest, "advance" moves it to the target stage.\n  5. Logic: add requirements (who may take or advance the quest) and rewards for the selected stage.\n  6. Validation: press Validate, fix every error, then Publish.\n\nSTATUS\n  [DRAFT] - editable, not visible to players.\n  [PUB]   - live for players. Any further edit returns it to Draft, so publish again when you are done.\n  [OFF]   - disabled. Delete is a soft delete: the file is kept for recovery.\n\nNOTES\n  Green topics only appear for players who satisfy the requirements of the current stage.\n  A choice needs both a target stage and the "advance" action to actually move the quest.\n  Rewards fire once, when the player enters the stage that owns them.
